# Which snip-36-prover-backend release strkd bundles into the desktop app.
#
# Single source of truth for the prover version, read by the CI release workflow
# and the staging scripts.
#
# ── UNVERIFIED BUMP: v1.1.3 -> v1.2.2 (2026-07-02) — needs live re-verification ──
#   Sepolia upgraded to protocol 0.14.3, which the old RC.6 stack (v1.1.3 / PROOF0)
#   CANNOT parse ("Invalid Starknet version: [0,14,3]" — every prove fails). v1.2.2
#   is the newest release and bumped the sequencer, so it's the candidate for 0.14.3
#   support. This bump is a TRY-AND-VERIFY, not a confirmed fix:
#     1. Does v1.2.2 actually parse 0.14.3 block headers? (prove a recent Sepolia tx)
#     2. Does the CURRENT (post-0.14.3-upgrade) Sepolia verifier accept its proof?
#        v1.2.x emitted "PROOF1", which the JUNE verifier REJECTED (node error 69) —
#        but the verifier was very likely upgraded alongside 0.14.3, so that pin
#        rationale is now stale. CONFIRM by prove + submit of a proof-carrying invoke
#        on Sepolia before trusting this pin.
#   If v1.2.2 does NOT support 0.14.3, this is blocked upstream — file a
#   snip-36-prover-backend issue for 0.14.3 support and revert this bump.
#
# STAGING: v1.2.x PREBUILT binaries are relocatable (unlike v1.1.3, which had to be
# built from source + patched), so stage-prover-prebuilt.sh is the fast path.
# `snip36 setup --prebuilt` pulls the deps set matched to the CLI (deps-v7 for the
# v1.2.x line). stage-prover-source.sh still works but is the slow (~30-40 min) path.
#
# See docs/project/status.md and memory prover-proof-format-pin / strkd-dinner-merge.
#
# Releases: https://github.com/starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend/releases
SNIP36_REPO=starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend
SNIP36_RELEASE=v1.2.2
